# Normalize to LF in the repository. The Makefile and shell hooks must stay LF in
# the working copy too: they are run by GNU make and bash, and this repo is built
# on Windows but reviewed on macOS/Linux.
* text=auto

Makefile text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
uv.lock text eol=lf

# Fetched source documents are evidence, not source code. docs/08 §2 step 4 commits
# them "so the report is reproducible", and an answer key is validated against exact
# passages — so these must round-trip byte for byte, with whatever line endings the
# document actually had. Any rewriting here would shift the character offsets a
# citation points at.
data/searchbench/sources/** -text
